   "descriptions": [
    {
     "description": "This package contains the code and data for a new deep learning framework for the prediction of solar flares. The model is designed to forecast the probability of a >=M-class solar flare within a 24-hour window using time-series data from NASA's Solar Dynamics Observatory. This package provides the full model architecture, the training and testing scripts, and the processed data necessary to replicate the model's state-of-the-art performance, which achieves a True Skill Statistic (TSS) of 0.90.",
     "descriptionType": "Abstract"
    }
